      "text": "Step 4: Add the result of the rotation back to $c$ to find $w$.\n\nFirst, convert $z$ and $c$ into complex numbers:\n\\[ z = 2 + \\sqrt{2} - (3 + 3\\sqrt{2})i = 2 + \\sqrt{2} - 3i - 3\\sqrt{2}i \\]\n\\[ c = 2 - 3i \\]\n\nThe vector from $c$ to $z$ is:\n\\[ z - c = (2 + \\sqrt{2} - 3i - 3\\sqrt{2}i) - (2 - 3i) = \\sqrt{2} - 3\\sqrt{2}i \\]\n\nTo rotate this vector by $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ counter-clockwise, we use the rotation matrix:\n\\[ \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4} & -\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\\\ \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} & \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\end{pmatrix} \\]\n\nApplying this to the vector $\\sqrt{2} - 3\\sqrt{2}i$:\n\\[ \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -3\\sqrt{2} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} + (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\cdot (-3\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot (-3\\sqrt{2}) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + 3 \\\\ 1 - 3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} \\]\n\nSo, the rotated vector is $4 - 2i$. Adding this back to $c$:\n\\[ w = c + (4 - 2i) = (2 - 3i) + (4 - 2i) = 6 - 5i \\]",
